# The vendored schema is a byte-for-byte copy of the canonical specification and
# its sha-256 is recorded in schema/SOURCE.json. Git must never rewrite its line
# endings: on a Windows checkout with core.autocrlf=true the file would change
# bytes, break the recorded checksum, and be published that way.
schema/agent-manifest-v1.0.schema.json -text

# Everything else is normalised to LF in the repository and in the tarball, so
# the package is identical whichever platform it was packed on.
* text=auto eol=lf
